A Component Diagram is a UML structural diagram that represents the organization and dependencies of different components or modules within a software system.

What does it show in Lord of Realms?

It divides the game into different functional modules.
- Presentation Layer: Handles the graphical user interface.
- Game Controller: Controls the overall game execution.
- Story Module: Manages story scenes and progression.
- Player Module: Manages player attributes and cultivation.
- Inventory Module: Handles items and inventory operations.
- Combat Module: Manages combat logic and damage calculations.
It also shows how these components communicate and depend on one another.

Purpose: To understand the high-level architecture and modular organization of the application.
